      en: "Lake Buir, located in eastern Mongolia's Dornod Province, covers 615 km² (375 km² within Mongolia). It is a shallow lake with a maximum depth of 10 m, fed by the Kherlen River and connected to China's Lake Hulun via the Khalkhin Gol River. The lake is a major fishery, yielding over 2,000 tons of fish annually, including Mongolian redfin and pike. It is a Ramsar wetland, supporting migratory birds like swans, geese, and cranes. Ice cover lasts from November to April. The area was a battlefield in the 1939 Soviet-Japanese conflict.",
